{"id": "EUVD-2026-96619", "enisaUuid": "7fc05cf6-9963-33cb-a4ad-16f86c20f048", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to send template notifications by calling POST /sys/api/sendTemplateAnnouncement. Low-privileged attackers can supply forged sender, recipients, title, and template parameters to deliver messages appearing to come from admin or system accounts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:00:17", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_api_credential_family.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/api/controller/SystemApiController.java#L62-L65", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-api-sendtemplateannouncement"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cmc8-rw33-2cqp", "CVE-2026-108680"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "732e2453-9d01-3ee7-b13d-22ef09b5f6c0", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5b11952e-0f3b-3930-a070-eba9beec835c", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}